Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 06:01:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PS5-ECAM's Switch side: its loading screen from the first
 frame, the whole in-game menu, rooms, and back to PS5-ECAM

PS5-ECAM's loading screen is drawn from the first loading frame: PresentLoading gives its drawing the
instance too, which only Composite did, so ProsperoEden's loading screen showed for the whole load
and PS5-ECAM's for its last second.

A game PS5-ECAM started (--rom with --return) never ends at ProsperoEden's launcher: one that is not
found, fails to start or stops with an error goes back to PS5-ECAM, a home screen tile's too, with
why in PS5-ECAM's result file (its port/eden/ingame.h), and a crash restart starts PS5-ECAM's eboot
first. An earlier crash, which PS5-ECAM says, no longer keeps its game from starting.

The in-game menu changes, at once: anti-aliasing and FSR's sharpening (read as each frame is
presented), the performance overlay (ShowHud, nothing saved), docked or handheld (the game told, as
desktop Eden does), the controller type (each player connected again with it), vibration and the
sticks' deadzone (Pad::SetDeadzone). Amiibo: Eden's virtual_amiibo engine, which the emulated
controllers' NFC reads, is built into the pad library, and a dump is loaded while the game looks
for one. The room PS5-ECAM's Multiplayer page chose (--set room_host=..., room_port, room_name,
room_nickname, room_password) is joined before the game starts, and the menu shows who is in it.
The session's new settings: anti_aliasing, fsr_sharpening, deadzone, controller.
